The independent differential test found zero divergence on the documented single-space token language, but exposed a boundary discrepancy with the trusted canonical on repeated or edge spaces (for example, canonical returns `{"": 1, "a": 1}` for `" a"`, while the candidate returns `{"a": 1}`). I’ll preserve this visibly and judge whether those strings are inside the stated contract; the proof reconstruction proceeds independently.
