codex
The false-result mutation built cleanly and failed on the intended residual (`pyInt(1)` versus the mutated `pyInt(2)`), and a mutation inside the executed `histogramProgram()` body also invalidated the main theorem. So the proof is discriminating and body-sensitive. The remaining defects are substantive: an unguarded `str.split()` model has a concrete real-Python counterexample, and the universal main theorem closes only after importing two loop equations whose complete match domains were never proved.
